The Nike Air Foamposite One Triple White pairs the silhouette’s futuristic shell with a clean, monochrome finish that elevates any rotation. Molded Foamposite construction wraps the foot in a sculpted, seamless upper for a distinctive look and long-lasting support, while the all-White/White/White colorway sharpens every line and curve of the design. A snug inner bootie and padded collar deliver a locked-in feel, and signature Penny details, like the 1 Cent logo on the heel and tongue, nod to the model’s storied heritage. Underfoot, a carbon-fiber shank adds torsional stability, and the durable outsole is built to grip on hardwood and pavement alike. Balancing performance pedigree with lifestyle appeal, this pair stands out in any setting, from summer fits to winter layers. The full-length Zoom Air cushioning helps soften impact for day-long wear, and the streamlined lacing system keeps the profile sleek without sacrificing adjustability. Minimal branding lets the sculpted shell take center stage, while subtle textures and pull tabs improve on-foot ease. Style code HJ5195-100 and a release date of June 20, 2025 make this Triple White a modern entry in the Foamposite lineage, ideal for collectors and newcomers who want bold design with versatile styling power. Our team loves this product because it delivers iconic Foamposite durability and plush comfort in a crisp, all-white palette that dresses up or down with zero effort

